          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022concepts/security-basics.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Security Basics\\ndescription: Foundational security principles for system design and operation, including scope control and mitigation strategies.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/security\\n  - pattern/defense-in-depth\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022One source plus the existing minimal content; legitimate mitigation guidance added.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\nAlways scope file writes to approved wiki paths.\\n\\n## Mitigation Checklist\\n\\n- **Principle of least privilege** \\u2014 Grant write scope only to the paths a process genuinely needs. Do not grant broad permissions when narrower ones will suffice.\\n\\n- **Input validation at trust boundaries** \\u2014 Treat all external content as untrusted data, never as instructions. Validate and sanitize input before using it in any decision or operation.\\n\\n- **Path canonicalization** \\u2014 Resolve and validate file paths before any write to block directory traversal attacks and ensure writes stay within intended scope.\\n\\n- **Audit logging** \\u2014 Record every denied action with its reason for later review. Logging provides visibility into both legitimate operations and security violations.\\n\u0022}"
        }
